      "message": "CBI is board ID 1 for current boards.\n\ni think what you\u0027re asking for is to assert that the *gpio.inc\nrevision used matches the board revision. we don\u0027t have that and\ni\u0027m updating *gpio.inc to rev 2 incrementally.\n\nit doesn\u0027t really help to check for board ID 2 because what matters\nis the revision of *gpio.inc used as well. the assumption is that\nGPIO_xyx is always correct for the most recent \"ToT\" board. \n\nthe logic is this: given the latest *gpio.inc definitions,\nwe must use symbol GPIO_ID1_xyz to refer to the relevant GPIO pin\non board ID 1. on newer boards, use the customary GPIO_xyz symbol. \n\n* board ID 0 is not supported.\n* all the GPIO_ID1_* symbols and handling should be removed when we\n  decide to drop support for board ID 1.",
